From 0bb206aa5d709f681ab8b7f3824a8b6bfe16fe6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:30:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Network settings: per-board hostname (default pico-<last 4
 hex of the board id>) and optional static IP

New config items HOSTNAME / IPADDR / NETMASK / GATEWAY / DNS (CONFIG.TXT and the settings UI,
right column). Empty IPADDR keeps DHCP; empty NETMASK is 255.255.255.0, empty DNS is the gateway.
They are stored after the v4 items with a "NET1" mark, so the magic stays v4 and older firmware
still reads the settings (it drops the new items when it writes them back).
net_setup() runs right after cyw43_arch_enable_sta_mode(), before the join, so DHCP already
sends the hostname. status starts with host=<name>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
